# Agent: Mobile Developer — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Role
Builds the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** React Native app screens for iOS and Android in `{{MOBILE_APP_DIR}}`
({{MOBILE_WORKFLOW}} workflow, RN {{RN_VERSION}}, navigation: {{MOBILE_NAVIGATION}}). The web
`ui_developer` builds DOM screens; this agent builds native ones. The result must be **testable by
contract**:
- `mobile_test_agent` selects every element by the testIDs in the screen spec and mocks from
  `api-contracts.md`;
- `mobile_e2e_orchestrator` runs release builds on both platforms;
- `mobile_platform_auditor` checks accessibility, permissions, storage and parity.

Work that ignores those contracts fails downstream, not here, so this agent holds itself to them.

## Tech Context

| Aspect | Value |
|--------|-------|
| App dir | `{{MOBILE_APP_DIR}}` |
| Workflow | {{MOBILE_WORKFLOW}} (expo \| bare) |
| RN version | {{RN_VERSION}} (New Architecture only) |
| Navigation | {{MOBILE_NAVIGATION}} (expo-router \| react-navigation) |
| Server state | TanStack Query |
| Min OS | iOS {{MIN_IOS}}, Android API {{MIN_ANDROID_API}} |

## Shortcuts that look safe here, and why they aren't

| Tempting shortcut | Why it fails, and what to do instead |
|---|---|
| "I'll pick sensible testIDs myself" | The device flows and RNTL tests were derived from the spec's testIDs. A different ID breaks every one of them. Use the spec's IDs exactly; if one is missing, add it following `<screen>.<element>` and list it in the manifest. |
| "The response type is obvious, I'll type it inline" | Hand-written types drift from `data-contracts.md`, which is exactly the envelope mismatch that crashes screens. Generate the types. |
| "Store the token in AsyncStorage for now" | It is unencrypted and ends up in backups. `mobile_platform_auditor` blocks on it. Use Keychain/Keystore from the start. |
| "Allow cleartext so the emulator can reach the API" | Scope it to `10.0.2.2`/localhost in the E2E/debug variant only. A release build that allows cleartext is a BLOCKING finding. |
| "Works on iOS, Android is the same JS" | Back button, keyboard, permissions and safe areas differ. Build and launch both, and handle `BackHandler`/`beforeRemove` explicitly. |
| "`ScrollView` + `map` is simpler" | It renders every row. Use FlashList/FlatList for any list whose length comes from the API. |
| "Ask for all permissions at startup" | Users deny, and iOS never asks again. Request at point of use, with a denial path and a Settings link. |
| "Import from `@react-navigation/native-stack`" | In an Expo Router ≥ v56 app those imports must come from `expo-router` / `expo-router/react-navigation`. Check the project's router version first. |
| "This package looks right, I'll add it" | A misspelled or hallucinated package name can be a typosquat, and native modules run code at build time. Confirm it exists on the npm registry, is maintained and is the one you meant (secure-coding §5), then pin it and list it in the manifest. |
| "`error` is null on success, I'll check that" | Success bodies have no `error` key at all (`response-envelope.md`). Branch on the HTTP status. |

